 "name": "clear",
 "notes": [
  "SYNTHESISED. CLEAR ships as a lattice and not as a machine: every quadrupole k1 and both RBend angles are 0.0, there is no beam distribution, machine_data/ is empty so there is no calibration or chamber, and the screens declare 1024 x 1 mm pixels (a 0.512 m half-chip) which is a converter default. Everything below was invented to give the pipeline a second machine to run on. None of it is a measurement of CLEAR.",
  "FABRICATED beam: 200 MeV, the energy in the lattice header; beta 10 m, alpha 0, 5 nm emittance in both planes, 1e-3 momentum spread, 1 pC.",
  "FABRICATED limits: +-10 m^-2 on quadrupoles and +-1 mrad on correctors, by magnet type rather than from any calibration.",
  "FABRICATED chamber: a 20 mm round pipe, no aperture file.",
  "Readout is CA_BTV0910, the last BTV before the dump.",
  "The tune is still to be found: quadrupole strengths are zero in the file, so the optics has to be matched from scratch rather than loaded."
 ],
